7. Formal Verification Roadmap

We outline the verification strategy in Isabelle/HOL.

1. Base protocol. Carr et al. (2022) mechanised safety of HotStuff in Agda; we reformulate the invariants in Isabelle/HOL. Liveness remains unmechanised globally; we assume it for the base protocol and prove that the monitor preserves it.
2. Safety shield. Lemma B.1 (shield correctness) is proved by model‑checking the shield automaton against the safe states. The factored composition theorem (Theorem 4.1) is formalised using simulation relations.
3. Liveness inheritance. A timed LTL proof shows that if the base protocol satisfies \Box\Diamond \text{block\_confirmed} under partial synchrony, then the shielded system does as well, because the monitor overrides after bounded idle rounds.
4. Compositional safety. The RL agent, when filtered by \sigma_s, cannot leave the safe region; thus \Box \varphi_{\text{safety}} holds for the composite system.

Full proof outlines appear in Appendix D.

